common: add missing <ctype.h> include for tolower()

gattlib_common_adapter.c's stricmp() calls tolower() without including
<ctype.h>. GCC >= 14 (this project's Bootlin toolchain) treats an
implicit function declaration as a hard error, not a warning, so 0.7.2
fails to build:

    common/gattlib_common_adapter.c:15:17: error: implicit declaration
    of function 'tolower' [-Wimplicit-function-declaration]

Fixed upstream after the 0.7.2 tag (gattlib master's
common/gattlib_common_adapter.c already has this include, in the same
place); backported here since we're pinned to the 0.7.2 release.
Confirmed against a real cross-build with this toolchain.

--- a/common/gattlib_common_adapter.c
+++ b/common/gattlib_common_adapter.c
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
  * Copyright (c) 2021-2024, Olivier Martin <olivier@labapart.org>
  */

+#include <ctype.h>
+
 #include "gattlib_internal.h"

 // Keep track of the allocated adapters to avoid an adapter to be freed twice.
